┗┻┛┗┻┛┗━╸╹ ╹┗━╸  ╹┗━┛   ┗━┛┗━╸┗┛

multiple-choice questions for https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF


three readouts of the same forward pass, one model, one server:

    jev_v1   read the odds of every answer letter off the next token, no generation
    jev_v2   a grammar allows only the answer letters, greedy, no odds
    plain    unconstrained, the model writes what it wants, we fish the letter out

    llm.decide(state, "did the deployment succeed?", ["yes", "no", "unclear"])
    -> {"yes": 0.91, "no": 0.03, "unclear": 0.06}


quick demo:

    $ uv run example.py


benchmark, 58 graded items over one incident report, with and without
thinking first, on a 3090 Ti:

    $ uv run bench.py

    mode          accuracy  p(expected)   s/item   total s
    ------------------------------------------------------
    jev-v1          94.8%        0.896     0.49      28.7
    jev-v1 think  100.0%        1.000     3.49     202.4
    jev-v2          94.8%            -     0.34      19.5
    jev-v2 think  100.0%            -     3.46     200.4
    plain           89.7%            -     0.37      21.2
    plain think    100.0%            -     3.51     203.4
    ------------------------------------------------------
    jev-v1 and jev-v2 pick the same answer on 100.0% of items, think=False
    jev-v1 and jev-v2 pick the same answer on 100.0% of items, think=True
    jev-v1 and plain pick the same answer on 84.5% of items, think=False
    jev-v1 and plain pick the same answer on 100.0% of items, think=True

jev-v1 and jev-v2 are the same decision: argmax of the next token. v2 is
faster because it skips the top-k dump that v1 needs to read the odds. v1
earns that only if you use the odds, e.g. to think just on the uncertain
ones. both beat sampling an unconstrained answer by five points, and
thinking gets everything to 100% at ten times the cost.


References:

- OpenJev, the same idea on a 4B model: https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/openjev
- Jev, the closed service it reproduces: https://typesafe.ai
- Qwen3.8-27B: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B
